 ,{s: 'circulatory disease', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_57b67a9c7798c919', doc: 'pubmed/28118530.txt', start: 1971, end: 2120, evidence: 'The health conditions most frequently associated with hospital readmission were diabetes mellitus, pulmonary disease, arrhythmias, and heart disease.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:11+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'death or readmission', fact: 'f_0aa1ee9bf0ab36f9', doc: 'pubmed/28203070.txt', start: 1244, end: 1708, evidence: 'In multivariate analysis, age (hazard ratio [HR] 1.03, 95% CI 1.02-1.05; P<0.0001), severity of airflow obstruction (forced expiratory volume in 1 s <30%; HR 4.65, 95% CI 1.42-15.1; P=0.01), diabetes (HR 1.47, 95% CI 1.003-2.16; P=0.048), cancer (HR 2.79, 95% CI 1.68-4.64; P<0.0001), creatinine (HR 1.003, 95% CI 1.0004-1.006; P=0.02), and respiratory rate (HR 1.03, 95% CI 1.003-1.05; P=0.028) on admission were significantly associated with the primary outcome.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:18+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'postdischarge sae and readmission', fact: 'f_d4a0079110ad4bc9', doc: 'pubmed/28455179.txt', start: 1536, end: 1787, evidence: 'The most important risk factors for predicting postdischarge SAE and readmission are predischarge SAE, dependent functional status, body mass index >40 kg/m2, smoking, diabetes, chronic steroid use, and American Society of Anesthesiologists class 3/4.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:29+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_f368dcd7ed7fd0ad', doc: 'pubmed/29107164.txt', start: 1257, end: 1432, evidence: 'In multivariable analysis, cannabis use and diabetes were predictors of both 30-day and 90-day readmission and older patients were uniquely susceptible to 30-day readmissions.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:56+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'hospital readmission within 90 days', fact: 'f_cbb5d97e8b3b47e0', doc: 'pubmed/29107164.txt', start: 1257, end: 1432, evidence: 'In multivariable analysis, cannabis use and diabetes were predictors of both 30-day and 90-day readmission and older patients were uniquely susceptible to 30-day readmissions.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:56+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'hypothyroidism', t: 'hospital readmission within 90 days', fact: 'f_23c4a831d6390371', doc: 'pubmed/29107164.txt', start: 1433, end: 1673, evidence: 'Risk factors for 90-day readmission included Medicare insurance, hypothyroidism, initial discharge to skilled nursing facility, and several index complications including bowel obstruction, gastrostomy, acute lung injury, and cerebral edema.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:31:56+00:00'}
