 ,{s: 'previous urinary tract infection', t: 'postoperative urinary retention', fact: 'f_7cc27ddd2388a30f', doc: 'pubmed/29447854.txt', start: 3140, end: 3465, evidence: 'Increased age (odds ratio [OR]=1.04; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.02-1.06; p<.001), benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) (OR=1.92; 95% CI, 1.32-2.78); p<.001), previous AKI (OR=3.29; 95% CI, 1.11-9.29; p=.025), and previous UTI (OR=1.69; 95% CI, 1.24-2.24; p<.001) significantly increased the probability of developing POUR.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:32:42+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_814a8faeaafec0e6', doc: 'pubmed/29478962.txt', start: 1275, end: 1429, evidence: 'Factors associated with an increased risk of readmission included diversion with neobladder, diabetes, prolonged surgical time, and obesity (all P < .01).', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:32:52+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_a54a7f66aa66baf8', doc: 'pubmed/29506837.txt', start: 1408, end: 1788, evidence: 'Multivariable analysis demonstrated that the occurrence of any postoperative complications, postoperative length of stay greater than 10 d, discharge to skilled nursing facility or home health care, combined resection with distal pancreatectomy and/or splenectomy, and patient comorbidities like diabetes mellitus and renal failure were independently associated with readmissions.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:32:55+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'chronic kidney disease', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_d7bf8d14917193b6', doc: 'pubmed/29506837.txt', start: 1408, end: 1788, evidence: 'Multivariable analysis demonstrated that the occurrence of any postoperative complications, postoperative length of stay greater than 10 d, discharge to skilled nursing facility or home health care, combined resection with distal pancreatectomy and/or splenectomy, and patient comorbidities like diabetes mellitus and renal failure were independently associated with readmissions.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:32:55+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'hospital readmission within 30 days', fact: 'f_98de6b3ae0d39c52', doc: 'pubmed/29949004.txt', start: 1832, end: 2083, evidence: 'In multivariable analysis, significant predictors of a higher readmission rate included diabetes (rate ratio [RR] 1.09, 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.03-1.15), congestive heart failure (RR 1.09, 1.003-1.18), and renal impairment (RR 1.35, 1.13-1.61).', confidence: 0.95, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:33:25+00:00'}
