 ,{s: 'diabetes', t: 'any complication', fact: 'f_040405335d6cf96c', doc: 'pubmed/41191374.txt', start: 1808, end: 2048, evidence: 'In those patients with diabetes, risk of any complication increased progressively from near normal (HbA1c level <6.0%; odds ratio [OR], 1.06; 95% CI, 1.00-1.11) to very poor glycemic control (HbA1c level >9.0%; OR, 1.32; 95% CI, 1.25-1.39).', confidence: 0.9, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T14:48:05+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'undiagnosed diabetes', t: 'medical complications', fact: 'f_c199b3c94615a842', doc: 'pubmed/41191374.txt', start: 2049, end: 2207, evidence: 'Undiagnosed diabetes was also associated with higher risks of medical complications (OR, 1.11; 95% CI, 1.04-1.18) and mortality (OR, 1.24; 95% CI, 1.07-1.42).', confidence: 0.95, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T14:48:05+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'undiagnosed diabetes', t: 'mortality', fact: 'f_085da1d4aeaca825', doc: 'pubmed/41191374.txt', start: 2049, end: 2207, evidence: 'Undiagnosed diabetes was also associated with higher risks of medical complications (OR, 1.11; 95% CI, 1.04-1.18) and mortality (OR, 1.24; 95% CI, 1.07-1.42).', confidence: 0.95, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T14:48:05+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'peptic ulcer disease', t: 'hospitalization costs', fact: 'f_00d87c9911b8bdc5', doc: 'pubmed/41671244.txt', start: 1471, end: 1663, evidence: 'Other significant predictors included skilled nursing facility discharge (SNF) (69.7-119.2% increase), primary procedures (11.0-53.8% increase), and peptic ulcer disease (66.1-135.8% increase.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T14:48:36+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'diabetic ketoacidosis', t: 'hospital admission', fact: 'f_f0fde2d40e0a2256', doc: 'pubmed/42036160.txt', start: 194, end: 409, evidence: 'Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA), Hyperosmolar Hyperglycemic State (HHS), and Hypoglycemia remain among the most serious acute complications of diabetes mellitus, often leading to hospitalization and increased morbidity.', confidence: 0.85, run: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2', runId: 'literature_extraction@9b00038fb5d2@gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', hash: '9b00038fb5d29957f1a4c7b2ee263124e8e3f36ea91607373a2d87988fc5b5cb', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.1-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T14:48:46+00:00'}
