 ,{s: 'insulin', t: 'pentamidine', fact: 'f_205c06d8d3503322', doc: 'openfda/insulin.txt', start: 25066, end: 25384, evidence: 'Pentamidine Prevention or Management Monitor blood glucose more frequently and modify AFREZZA dosage, as clinically indicated, when used concomitantly with these drugs. Mechanism and Clinical Effect(s) Concomitant use of pentamidine with AFREZZA may cause hypoglycemia, which may sometimes be followed by hyperglycemia', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:11:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'insulin', t: 'guanethidine', fact: 'f_fbda217f35106533', doc: 'openfda/insulin.txt', start: 25385, end: 25760, evidence: 'Beta-blockers, Clonidine, Guanethidine, and Reserpine Prevention or Management Monitor blood glucose more frequently and modify AFREZZA dosage, as clinically indicated, when used concomitantly with these drugs. Mechanism and Clinical Effect(s) Concomitant use of these drugs with AFREZZA may blunt the signs and symptoms of hypoglycemia, making it more difficult to recognize', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:11:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'insulin', t: 'reserpine', fact: 'f_8217a0f18712abe6', doc: 'openfda/insulin.txt', start: 25385, end: 25760, evidence: 'Beta-blockers, Clonidine, Guanethidine, and Reserpine Prevention or Management Monitor blood glucose more frequently and modify AFREZZA dosage, as clinically indicated, when used concomitantly with these drugs. Mechanism and Clinical Effect(s) Concomitant use of these drugs with AFREZZA may blunt the signs and symptoms of hypoglycemia, making it more difficult to recognize', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:11:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'insulin', fact: 'f_8be1ec58eb173dc8', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 18362, end: 18472, evidence: 'Hypoglycemia with Concomitant Use with Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues [see Warnings and Precautions ( 5.6 )]', confidence: 0.8, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'metformin', fact: 'f_2cdc680aa7975067', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 18668, end: 18896, evidence: 'Most common adverse reactions (incidence ≥5% of patients simultaneously started on sitagliptin and metformin and more commonly than in patients treated with placebo were diarrhea, upper respiratory tract infection, and headache.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'zituvimet', t: 'topiramate', fact: 'f_a4b331b93d3c93a6', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 30787, end: 31011, evidence: 'Concomitant use of these drugs with ZITUVIMET may increase the risk for lactic acidosis. Intervention: Consider more frequent monitoring of these patients. Examples: Topiramate, zonisamide, acetazolamide or dichlorphenamide.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
