 ,{s: 'glimepiride', t: 'hemolytic anemia', fact: 'f_1eaba6776489c9d5', doc: 'openfda/glimepiride.txt', start: 6839, end: 6893, evidence: 'Hemolytic anemia [see Warnings and Precautions (5.3) ]', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:05:48+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glimepiride', t: 'weight gain', fact: 'f_b20b604f641b572c', doc: 'openfda/glimepiride.txt', start: 10150, end: 10240, evidence: 'Glimepiride, like all sulfonylureas, can cause weight gain [see Clinical Studies (14.1) ].', confidence: 0.98, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:05:48+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glimepiride', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_ace415fdb1ca72e7', doc: 'openfda/glimepiride.txt', start: 16359, end: 16462, evidence: 'Pediatric Patients: Not recommended because of adverse effects on body weight and hypoglycemia ( 8.4 ).', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:05:48+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glimepiride', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_4b228e0326ccea9f', doc: 'openfda/glimepiride.txt', start: 16899, end: 17043, evidence: 'However, sulfonylureas (including glimepiride) cross the placenta and have been associated with neonatal adverse reactions such as hypoglycemia.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:05:48+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glimepiride', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_58f52482e97a7531', doc: 'openfda/glimepiride.txt', start: 21383, end: 21508, evidence: 'Glimepiride tablets are not recommended in pediatric patients because of its adverse effects on body weight and hypoglycemia.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:05:48+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_d5a906230eea8ea3', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 2717, end: 2816, evidence: 'There have been postmarketing cases of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, including fatal cases.', confidence: 0.98, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_3f66cb55f22c9092', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 6473, end: 6646, evidence: 'Administration of intravascular iodinated contrast agents in metformin-treated patients has led to an acute decrease in renal function and the occurrence of lactic acidosis.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_0bd5b73d098b9729', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 9294, end: 9496, evidence: 'Glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets are capable of producing hypoglycemia; therefore, proper patient selection, dosing, and instructions are important to avoid potential hypoglycemic episodes.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_56707f85a2948497', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 18958, end: 19338, evidence: 'Concomitant use of drugs that interfere with common renal tubular transport systems involved in the renal elimination of metformin (e.g., organic cationic transporter-2 [OCT2] / multidrug and toxin extrusion [MATE] inhibitors such as ranolazine, vandetanib, dolutegravir, and cimetidine) could increase systemic exposure to metformin and may increase the risk for lactic acidosis.', confidence: 0.8, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'topiramate', t: 'metabolic acidosis', fact: 'f_28d991e9ce2686f2', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 20323, end: 20537, evidence: 'Topiramate or other carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (e.g., zonisamide, acetazolamide or dichlorphenamide) frequently causes a decrease in serum bicarbonate and induce non-anion gap, hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_fc6e92d95a4ab9a9', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 24586, end: 24740, evidence: 'Prolonged severe hypoglycemia (4 to 10 days) has been reported in neonates born to mothers who were receiving a sulfonylurea drug at the time of delivery.', confidence: 0.8, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_95b87555d8e17a11', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 25444, end: 25696, evidence: 'Because the potential for hypoglycemia in nursing infants may exist, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.', confidence: 0.7, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_9a0cc44f61ee9533', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 25444, end: 25696, evidence: 'Because the potential for hypoglycemia in nursing infants may exist, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.', confidence: 0.7, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'upper respiratory infection', fact: 'f_836cbd8cd369e112', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 28065, end: 28128, evidence: 'Upper respiratory infection 12 (7.1) 15 (8.5) 17 (9.9) 14 (8.1)', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'diarrhea', fact: 'f_0ba7be28892ce571', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 28129, end: 28170, evidence: 'Diarrhea 8 (4.7) 15 (8.5) 4 (2.3) 9 (5.2)', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'dizziness', fact: 'f_8f24759a48c4d776', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 28171, end: 28212, evidence: 'Dizziness 9 (5.3) 2 (1.1) 3 (1.7) 9 (5.2)', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'circulatory disease', fact: 'f_8a5f039f808d4683', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 28213, end: 28260, evidence: 'Hypertension 17 (10.0) 10 (5.6) 5 (2.9) 6 (3.5)', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'nausea/vomiting', fact: 'f_6d409ab000de4b90', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 28261, end: 28308, evidence: 'Nausea/vomiting 6 (3.5) 9 (5.1) 1 (0.6) 3 (1.7)', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'liver injury', fact: 'f_4c73d4ac73cba774', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 31556, end: 31774, evidence: 'Cholestatic and hepatocellular forms of liver injury accompanied by jaundice have been reported rarely in association with glipizide; glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets should be discontinued if this occurs.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'jaundice', fact: 'f_3cb48b0fdaf9e1e4', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 31556, end: 31774, evidence: 'Cholestatic and hepatocellular forms of liver injury accompanied by jaundice have been reported rarely in association with glipizide; glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets should be discontinued if this occurs.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_0fd530069899e00f', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 38804, end: 38989, evidence: 'Generally, elderly, debilitated, and malnourished patients should not be titrated to the maximum dose of glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets to avoid the risk of hypoglycemia.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_d700bb094e42bbbd', doc: 'openfda/glipizide-and-metformin.txt', start: 38990, end: 39122, evidence: 'Monitoring of renal function is necessary to aid in prevention of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, particularly in the elderly.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:07:00+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_7ccdfe6be944e36f', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 2703, end: 2802, evidence: 'There have been postmarketing cases of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, including fatal cases.', confidence: 0.98, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_2ca2f72b309fa8f3', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 6459, end: 6632, evidence: 'Administration of intravascular iodinated contrast agents in metformin-treated patients has led to an acute decrease in renal function and the occurrence of lactic acidosis.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_6186e68a562a6cdb', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 9280, end: 9482, evidence: 'Glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets are capable of producing hypoglycemia; therefore, proper patient selection, dosing, and instructions are important to avoid potential hypoglycemic episodes.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hemolytic anemia', fact: 'f_06a15f6b7204dc9f', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 10535, end: 10668, evidence: 'Treatment of patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency with sulfonylurea agents can lead to hemolytic anemia.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'megaloblastic anemia', fact: 'f_1849c6b4375b6a36', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 14092, end: 14229, evidence: 'While megaloblastic anemia has rarely been seen with metformin therapy, if this is suspected, vitamin B 12 deficiency should be excluded.', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'topiramate', t: 'hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis', fact: 'f_2c414e58fa7d3a24', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 20309, end: 20523, evidence: 'Topiramate or other carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (e.g., zonisamide, acetazolamide or dichlorphenamide) frequently causes a decrease in serum bicarbonate and induce non-anion gap, hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'benign stromal uterine polyps', fact: 'f_4aa5526f28fead1f', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 22141, end: 22278, evidence: 'There was, however, an increased incidence of benign stromal uterine polyps in female rats treated with 900 mg/kg/day of metformin alone.', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_f4ca56c54594d099', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 25430, end: 25682, evidence: 'Because the potential for hypoglycemia in nursing infants may exist, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.', confidence: 0.8, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'upper respiratory infection', fact: 'f_3073664575434eab', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 28051, end: 28114, evidence: 'Upper respiratory infection 12 (7.1) 15 (8.5) 17 (9.9) 14 (8.1)', confidence: 0.8, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_46c1c493a0dc6687', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 29325, end: 29658, evidence: 'Hypoglycemia In a controlled initial therapy trial of glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets, 2.5 mg/250 mg and 2.5 mg/500 mg the numbers of patients with hypoglycemia documented by symptoms (such as dizziness, shakiness, sweating, and hunger) and a fingerstick blood glucose measurement ≤ 50 mg/dL were 5 (2.9%) for glipizide', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide', t: 'cholestatic and hepatocellular forms of liver injury accompanied by jaundice', fact: 'f_c9f6db0711dc7553', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 31542, end: 31760, evidence: 'Cholestatic and hepatocellular forms of liver injury accompanied by jaundice have been reported rarely in association with glipizide; glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets should be discontinued if this occurs.', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glipizide and metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_c5533f88d1d71fbb', doc: 'openfda/glipizide.txt', start: 38790, end: 38975, evidence: 'Generally, elderly, debilitated, and malnourished patients should not be titrated to the maximum dose of glipizide and metformin hydrochloride tablets to avoid the risk of hypoglycemia.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:08:34+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_2c3bfc107d31f09d', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 313, end: 454, evidence: 'Postmarketing cases of metformin-associated lactic acidosis have resulted in death, hypothermia, hypotension, and resistant bradyarrhythmias.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
