 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'resistant bradyarrhythmias', fact: 'f_6137f1e25df272b7', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 313, end: 454, evidence: 'Postmarketing cases of metformin-associated lactic acidosis have resulted in death, hypothermia, hypotension, and resistant bradyarrhythmias.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_6c1369d196664adc', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 4942, end: 5041, evidence: 'There have been postmarketing cases of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, including fatal cases.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'vitamin b12 deficiency', fact: 'f_63d2bad2edfa2c55', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 4759, end: 4799, evidence: 'Metformin may lower vitamin B 12 levels.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_7814540cd6a61ce4', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 7989, end: 8330, evidence: 'Drug interactions— The concomitant use of glyburide and metformin hydrochloride with specific drugs may increase the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis: those that impair renal function, result in significant hemodynamic change, interfere with acid-base balance, or increase metformin accumulation [ see Drug Interactions ( 7 ) ] .', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_38ef476cfe0c14be', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 11420, end: 11569, evidence: 'All sulfonylurea drugs, including glyburide and metformin hydrochloride, are capable of producing severe hypoglycemia [see Adverse Reactions ( 6 ) ].', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_4f473dd9f7fff91d', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 11570, end: 11701, evidence: 'Concomitant use of glyburide and metformin hydrochloride with other anti-diabetic medication can increase the risk of hypoglycemia.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'hemolytic anemia', fact: 'f_c5c76f08720ee7f0', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 14817, end: 15000, evidence: 'Treatment of patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency with sulfonylurea agents, including glyburide and metformin hydrochloride, can lead to hemolytic anemia.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'anemia', fact: 'f_1fcfbcb30f7643fa', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 15424, end: 15663, evidence: 'Such decrease, possibly due to interference with B 12 absorption from the B 12 -intrinsic factor complex, may be associated with anemia but appears to be rapidly reversible with discontinuation of metformin or vitamin B 12 supplementation.', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'glyburide and metformin', t: 'lactic acidosis', fact: 'f_3807ae21b48f1861', doc: 'openfda/glyburide-and-metformin.txt', start: 16246, end: 16397, evidence: 'The following adverse reactions are also discussed elsewhere in the labeling: Lactic Acidosis [see Boxed Warning and Warnings and Precautions ( 5.1 ) ]', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:09:57+00:00'}
