 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'diarrhea', fact: 'f_16bcb442150c07d0', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 18668, end: 18896, evidence: 'Most common adverse reactions (incidence ≥5% of patients simultaneously started on sitagliptin and metformin and more commonly than in patients treated with placebo were diarrhea, upper respiratory tract infection, and headache.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'upper respiratory tract infection', fact: 'f_9977d1ab98b719cf', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 18668, end: 18896, evidence: 'Most common adverse reactions (incidence ≥5% of patients simultaneously started on sitagliptin and metformin and more commonly than in patients treated with placebo were diarrhea, upper respiratory tract infection, and headache.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'headache', fact: 'f_b38b3e5dadb9f473', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 18668, end: 18896, evidence: 'Most common adverse reactions (incidence ≥5% of patients simultaneously started on sitagliptin and metformin and more commonly than in patients treated with placebo were diarrhea, upper respiratory tract infection, and headache.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_345bf046ba64cdce', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 25712, end: 26054, evidence: 'The overall incidence of reported adverse reactions of hypoglycemia in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on diet and exercise was 0.6% in patients given placebo, 0.6% in patients given sitagliptin alone, 0.8% in patients given metformin alone, and 1.6% in patients given sitagliptin in combination with metformin.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'metformin', t: 'hypoglycemia', fact: 'f_e6b83db54ef305e6', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 25712, end: 26054, evidence: 'The overall incidence of reported adverse reactions of hypoglycemia in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on diet and exercise was 0.6% in patients given placebo, 0.6% in patients given sitagliptin alone, 0.8% in patients given metformin alone, and 1.6% in patients given sitagliptin in combination with metformin.', confidence: 0.9, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'acute pancreatitis', fact: 'f_b8f350068cac3cdc', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 27283, end: 27569, evidence: 'In a pooled analysis of 19 double-blind clinical trials that included data from 10,246 patients randomized to receive sitagliptin 100 mg/day (N=5,429) or corresponding (active or placebo) control (N=4,817), the incidence of acute pancreatitis was 0.1 per 100 patient-years in each group', confidence: 0.85, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
 ,{s: 'sitagliptin', t: 'nasopharyngitis', fact: 'f_59b9b520573c8822', doc: 'openfda/metformin.txt', start: 27713, end: 27872, evidence: 'The most common adverse experience in sitagliptin monotherapy reported in ≥5% of patients and more commonly than in patients given placebo was nasopharyngitis.', confidence: 0.95, run: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277', runId: 'drug_label_extraction@fc3d922aa277@gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', hash: 'fc3d922aa27751cd23bc5136339e3e9669ebbfd16084612234d8ae7245fceda4', llm: 'gemini/gemini-3.5-flash-lite', policy: 'f20cdba4b6a0133d1db0677e5c18d6c31c2c50e396d718c04900094dffbe3b6a', ts: '2026-10-15T12:13:04+00:00'}
